         "id": "v2-2f0902af-p30-topic-j3-044013-j3-q-a",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "a",
         "prompt": "Find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y=2\\sin\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$ for $0\\le x\\le2\\pi$.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 35,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ and $x=\\frac{7\\pi}{6}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=0\\\\\\sin\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)&=0\\\\x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}&=0,\\ \\pi\\qquad\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\le\\frac{11\\pi}{6}\\right)\\\\x&=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\ \\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\end{align*}$$"
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-2f0902af-p30-topic-j3-044013-j3-q-b",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "b",
         "prompt": "Hence find the exact area of the region bounded by the curve and the $x$-axis between these two intercepts.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 50,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$4$ square units.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\int_{\\pi/6}^{7\\pi/6}2\\sin\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)dx\\\\&=\\left[-2\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right]_{\\pi/6}^{7\\pi/6}\\\\&=-2\\cos\\pi+2\\cos 0\\\\&=2+2\\\\&=4\\text{ square units}\\end{align*}$$"
         }
        }
       ],
