     "blockId": "p24-theory",
     "replacement": "Sometimes we cannot find the exact area under a curve, because:\n\n- there is no function rule, or\n- the function has no elementary primitive, for example $f(x)=e^{x^2}$.\n\nWe can then approximate the area by splitting it into trapeziums. This is often more accurate than using the same number of left- or right-endpoint rectangles in Riemann sums.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p24-theory",
